Local changes: extractor imports isolated plugin settings instead of image-wide
YouTube config. A small Python 3 compatibility module replaces the old Python 2
shim. Radio's wrapper supplies verified TLS, bounded downloads and a common
deadline. The Android device profile is updated; an explicit current public
VISIONOS fallback and native HLS master playback are added. Public client-profile
reference: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/blob/master/yt_dlp/extractor/youtube/_base.py
Highest-first combined-format ranking, adaptive HLS preference and bounded
lower-quality retry candidates are added. Sign-in demands are reported directly.
No global SSL/configuration mutations or external plugin installation.
The interpreter is otherwise retained from the pinned upstream source.

Paired DASH candidates are now selected per call, validated on both origins and
passed to a detected Exteplayer backend; image-global settings remain untouched.
Video format height ranks quality. Missing audio rejects a video-only candidate.
